                          Save's is at accounts.go:190-191.
  - Validate           -> accounts.go:121  vs accounts.go:192
  - OverlapWarnings(accts, existingCSVBasenames(s))
                       -> accounts.go:124  vs accounts.go:195  (identical args)
  - marshal            -> accounts.go:129  vs accounts.go:200
  - write              -> accounts.go:133 tx.WriteFile vs accounts.go:204 s.WriteFile
  - log each warning   -> accounts.go:136-138 vs accounts.go:179-181

Inspection alone is not evidence, so a checker-only probe was staged into the
package, run, and removed (it is NOT left in the repo; the source is kept at
/tmp/claude-1000/-home-darrell-work-agents2/6b77f711-9b6d-4e6e-ae1b-78859d900ee1/scratchpad/zz_checker_r1_warnings_test.go).
Command:
  cp .../zz_checker_r1_warnings_test.go internal/services/accounts/ && \
  go test -race -count=1 -v -run 'TestZZCheckerR1' ./internal/services/accounts/
The probe seeds a data dir containing usaa-checking-2026.csv and two accounts
("aaa" pattern "usaa", "bbb" pattern "*.csv") that both match it, redirects the
standard logger into a buffer, and compares the lines emitted by Save against
the lines emitted by Mutate(fn returning the same set).
Output:
  --- PASS: TestZZCheckerR1_MutateEmitsSameOverlapWarningsAsSave (0.00s)
      Save logged:   ["Warning: file \"usaa-checking-2026.csv\" matches multiple accounts (aaa, bbb); \"aaa\" wins by ID order"]
      Mutate logged: ["Warning: file \"usaa-checking-2026.csv\" matches multiple accounts (aaa, bbb); \"aaa\" wins by ID order"]
  --- PASS: TestZZCheckerR1_MutateNilStorageGuard (0.00s)
      Save(nil)=accounts: nil storage  Mutate(nil)=accounts: nil storage
  --- PASS: TestZZCheckerR1_MutateRunsValidate (0.00s)
      both rejected with: duplicate account ID "x"
  ok  budget2/internal/services/accounts  1.012s
The lead's stated deciding reason therefore holds on the merged tree: a
Mutate-based save emits byte-identical overlap warnings, the same nil-storage
error string, and the same Validate error as a direct Save.

MINOR, NON-BLOCKING NUANCE (recorded, not a criterion failure): Save logs its
warnings unconditionally, including when SaveWithWarnings returned an error
(accounts.go:178-182 loops over the returned warnings before returning err).
saveTx logs only after a successful tx.WriteFile (accounts.go:133-138), so on a
marshal or write failure the warnings are returned-but-unlogged. Success-path
behaviour, which is what the criterion asks about, is identical.

