4. Lock order correct, cannot deadlock                         => PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------
a) Package mutex OUTSIDE BeginShared:
   internal/services/accounts/accounts.go:84  mu.Lock()
   internal/services/accounts/accounts.go:85  defer mu.Unlock()
   internal/services/accounts/accounts.go:87  tx := s.BeginShared()
   internal/services/accounts/accounts.go:88  defer tx.Release()
   Command: grep -rn 'mu\.Lock|mu\.Unlock|BeginShared|BeginExclusive' internal/services/accounts/
   -- the only occurrences are those, in that order. Matches the order the
   storage doc comment pins (storage.go:619-626).

b) Nothing inside the held section calls the plain Storage write methods:
   loadTx uses tx.ReadFile (accounts.go:106); saveTx uses tx.WriteFile
   (accounts.go:133). SharedTx.WriteFile routes to s.writeFileLocked
   (storage.go:652-657), which does NOT re-take dataMu; Storage.WriteFile
   (storage.go:295-303) does take dataMu.RLock and is never called inside the
   section. Storage's read path takes no dataMu at all (storage.go:226-251),
   as the SharedTx doc comment states, so tx.ReadFile is safe. The only other
   in-section work is pure computation plus filepath.Glob in
   existingCSVBasenames (accounts.go:326-337) and log.Printf.

c) No held section spans a call into another service. ensureSnapshot is
   OUTSIDE the transaction: internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/anchor.go:199
   (`paths, snapNote, err := ensureSnapshot(deps, accountsFile)`) precedes the
   Mutate call at anchor.go:209, and the comment at anchor.go:203-208 states
   the reason. The four other Mutate callbacks (handlers.go:189, 252, 303,
   433; register.go:146) contain only slice manipulation, sort.Slice and
   time.Now — no service calls, verified by reading each callback body in
   `git diff HEAD -- internal/handlers/accounts/handlers.go`.

d) No inverse edge (dataMu held -> wait on accounts.mu):
   Command: grep -rn 'BeginShared()\|BeginExclusive()' internal/ --include=*.go | grep -v '^internal/services/storage/'
   Non-test holders are: internal/services/dataloader/loader.go:116 and
   internal/services/restore/restore.go:237. restore.go does not reference the
   accounts package at all (it is not among the importers listed by
   `grep -rn 'services/accounts"' internal/ --include=*.go | grep -v _test.go`).
   dataloader touches accounts only at loader.go:301 (accounts.Load) and :325
   (accounts.Find/MatchFile), both inside LoadDataContext (func at :276), which
   never calls beginWrite; and accounts.Load takes no lock in any case. So no
   code path holds dataMu and then waits on accounts.mu.

e) Empirical: the oracle's TestZZOracleR1_MutateExcludesTheExclusiveHold passes
   (the exclusive hold is refused for the whole 300ms the section is open and
   IS granted within 5s of Mutate returning, i.e. the hold does not leak), and
   the whole suite is green under -race with no deadlock/timeout.

